# A counted squeeze's bias is priced per draw.
#
# The adapter multiplies a challenge's statistical distance by its vector
# count, and no configuration in the tree could observe that factor until this
# one: the counted challenges the families emit sample a power-of-two space
# out of a power-of-two squeeze domain, where the distance is zero, and every
# challenge with a nonzero distance elsewhere is scalar. A wrong factor there
# would have priced every future counted squeeze with nothing turning red.
#
# The fixture is the shipped Fiat-Shamir sumcheck with one challenge added:
# three draws of a seven-value space through an eight-symbol squeeze. Both
# codec-bias facts move, and the differential against the unmodified artifact
# is what isolates the count -- the sumcheck's own rounds are common to both,
# so what the subtraction leaves is exactly this challenge's contribution.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/../Encoding/sumcheck-fs.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/plain.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/Inputs/sumcheck-fs-counted.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/counted.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/plain.artifacts %t/plain.mlirbc
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/counted.artifacts %t/counted.mlirbc
# RUN: %python %S/../Evidence/Inputs/retarget_request.py %S/Inputs/sumcheck-fs-request.json %t/plain.artifacts %t/plain.req.json
# RUN: %python %S/../Evidence/Inputs/retarget_request.py %S/Inputs/sumcheck-fs-request.json %t/counted.artifacts %t/counted.req.json
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%t/plain.req.json -o=%t/plain.out.json %t/plain.mlirbc > /dev/null
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%t/counted.req.json -o=%t/counted.out.json %t/counted.mlirbc \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNOWNED

# The added challenge belongs to no reduction, so the artifact-global bias
# facts see it while no rule prices its round. The two accountings disagree
# about scope on purpose; the judgment is where that becomes visible.
# UNOWNED: belongs to no transformer this derivation covers

# Both bias facts move by exactly three draws of this challenge's distance:
# the sum in the constant, the max in the linear coefficient. The expected
# value comes from the reference twin's own derivation of the per-draw
# distance, so the factor is checked against a number this leg did not
# compute.
# RUN: %if uv %{ %uv python -m oracle.parity construction-bias toy_duplex ts_be8 7 > %t/per-draw.json %}
# RUN: %if uv %{ %python %S/Inputs/counted_bias_delta.py %t/plain.out.json %t/counted.out.json %t/per-draw.json 3 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DELTA %}
# DELTA: constant moved by 3 draws: yes
# DELTA-NEXT: linear coefficient moved by 3 draws: yes

# The bias in the display, which is where a reader meets it. The unmodified
# artifact's constant is zero -- its challenge space divides the squeeze
# domain exactly -- and zero is shown rather than omitted, because an omitted
# line and a zero line would read alike and whether the bias is zero is the
# fact a reader comparing two configurations is after.
# RUN: zkc-derive --headline --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%t/plain.req.json -o=/dev/null %t/plain.mlirbc | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ZERO
# ZERO: headline term constant: 0
